-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",28,{
[865]="7006C6F4\n1\tLearn about the Tomb of Nirgambâr from denizens of Jirush ([see journal]/6)\tRaphûz has chosen to pursue the cost Igbâl put on pursuing Ashâmi's hand. He wants to learn all he can from the people of Jirush about the Tomb of Nirgambâr before he ventures there.\n2\tTalk to Raphûz\tYou visited many of the inhabitants of Jirush and enquired about the Tombs of Nirgambâr. It sounds like a terrible place. You should return to Raphûz at his camp in Jirush with the information.\n",
[866]="70060965\n1\tDefeat half-orcs in Thelgarth (total: 8)\tThe half-orcs of Thelgarth are sure to have Maervellon's lucky talisman. Sure they are.\n2\tTalk to Maervellon outside Thelgarth\tMaervellon remains outside the fortress of Thelgarth, in the Angle.\n",
[867]="70060964\n1\tDefeat wargs in the Angle (total: 6)\tWargs can be found among the old burrows of Glynafon, in the Angle.\n2\tTalk to Maervellon at Glynafon\tMaervellon is near the old hobbit-burrows of Glynafon, in the Angle.\n",
[868]="70060963\n1\tDefeat Orcs in the Angle and keep an eye out for Maervellon's talisman (total: 10)\tSlay Orcs within the Angle and keep an eye out for the lost talisman.\n2\tTalk to Maervellon outside Eitheldir\tReturn to Maervellon outside the ruins of Eitheldir.\n",
[869]="7004E75D\n1\tDwarves willing to share rumours can be found along the main passage and in the upper and lower wings of King Thorin's hall, in Erebor. Learn what you can of the rumours in Erebor.\t\n2\tReturn to King Thorin\tYou should return to King Thorin in Erebor with news of the rumours you have heard.\n3\tFetch Spall the Lore-master\tSpall can be found in the great hall of Erebor. You should go inform Spall the Lore-master that King Thorin wishes to speak with him.\n4\tReturn to King Thorin\tYou should return to King Thorin in Erebor now that you have summoned Spall the Lore-master.\n",
[870]="7002C60A\n1\tComplete Finnvarth is Lost\030Complete Bíli is Missing\tYou should rescue the two missing dwarves, Finnvarth and Bíli, who disappeared somewhere to the east of the old sawmill in the Limlight Gorge.\n2\tTalk to Armund in the Limlight Gorge\tYou should speak with Armund in the old sawmill in the Limlight Gorge.\n3\tComplete Gerfinn Has Gone Astray\030Complete Darfi Has Wandered Off\030Complete Dolmund Has Vanished\tThree more of Armund's companions remain missing within the Gorge, and morale among the band of dwarves remains low as Armund continues to drive them to complete the ill-advised venture.\n4\tTalk to Dolmund\tYou should speak with Dolmund in the old sawmill in the Limlight Gorge.\n5\tTalk to Armund\tConvince Armund to give up the Sawmill.\n6\tSpeak with Dolmund\tSpeak with Dolmund at the Sawmill in Limlight Gorge.\n",
[871]="70068C6D\n1\tMeet with Elder Roshat in Khûtra\tSpeak with Elder Roshat about the strange disease afflicting Khûtra.\n",
[872]="70068395\n1\tMeet with Elder Madag in Khûtra\tMeet with Elder Madag about the strange disease afflicting Khûtra.\n",
[873]="7006906D\n1\tCollect shellfish from traps (total: 10)\030Collect oversized crab claws from great crabs (total: 8)\tAid the harvest on the Shield Isles by collecting shellfish from traps and fighting great crabs for their claws.\n2\tFind and defeat the crab cast-mother\tDefeat the crab cast-mother.\n",
[874]="700033BD\n1\tTalk to Milo Bolger\tMilo Bolger is at a farm east of Budgeford, keeping an eye on the wolves in the nearby ruins. Linda Bolger came to Budgeford looking for someone to help with the wolf problem. She has asked you to speak with her husband, Milo.\n2\tDefeat wolves (total: 8)\tThe wolves can be found east of Milo and Linda Bolger's farm, among the ruins. Linda Bolger sent you to speak with her husband, Milo, in regards to the wolves that have entered the Shire. Milo asked you to thin the pack before they can become a greater threat.\n3\tTalk to Milo Bolger\tMilo Bolger is keeping an eye on the wolves east of Budgeford. Milo will be pleased to hear that you have reduced the number of wolves the Hobbits of Budgeford will need to deal with.\n",
[875]="7006595E\n1\tCollect tart berries (total: 8)\tKúmri has asked you to pick some berries outside of Ost Anglebed. Find tart berries in the fields east of Ost Anglebed.\n2\tTalk to Kúmri\tYou have found enough tart berries to satisfy Kúmri. Deliver the tart berries to Kúmri.\n",
[876]="70047F58\n1\tParticipate in Spring Festival activities (total: 10)\tEvery day there is something to do for the Spring Festival. Celebrate the change of a season and participate in the many Spring Festival activities at the Bree-land Festival Grounds, Bree-town, Duillond in Ered Luin, Brockenborings in the Shire, and Clegur in Swanfleet.\n2\tTalk to Sergeant Tom\030Talk to Rhudamer Hirtul\tYour hosts would like to thank you for your participation in the Spring Festival today. You should talk to either Sergeant Tom at the Bree-land Festival Grounds or Rhudamer Hirtul near the Stable-master in Clegur.\n",
[877]="70043B46\n1\tTalk to Faelleron in north-west Lothlórien\tFaelleron is beneath a flet on the north-western edge of the Golden Wood, near the border with Fanuidhol. Bingo wants to prove that he is not afraid of Orcs, and wants you to volunteer the two of you to fight the foes of Lórien in Fanuidhol.\n2\tDefeat Orcs or goblins in Fanuidhol (total: 8)\tYou have agreed to fight the Orcs in Fanuidhol, north-west of Lothlórien, for Faelleron.\n3\tTalk to Faelleron on the north-west border of the Golden Wood\tFaelleron is south-east of Fanuidhol, on the border of Lothlórien. You have defeated some of the Orcs that threaten the Golden Wood, and should now return to Faelleron.\n4\tTalk to Bingo on the north-west border of the Golden Wood, near Faelleron\tBingo is south-east of Fanuidhol, on the border of Lothlórien, with Faelleron. You have defeated some of the Orcs that threaten the Golden Wood, and should now return to Bingo.\n5\tTalk to Calengoth on the docks\tCalengoth is at the docks of Lothlórien, west of Imlad Lalaith. You have attained the permission to fight the enemies of Lothlórien for which Bingo hoped, and now he wants you to show it to Calengoth at the docks.\n6\tGain access to Mirkwood by completing 'Book 9, Foreword: The Dark Shore' by speaking to Calengoth and completing his quest chain through 'Hilltop Assault.'\tBingo has obtained permission to follow the Golden Host into Mirkwood. Now you should gain access to Mirkwood by completing 'Book 9, Foreword: The Dark Shore' by speaking to Calengoth at the docks in Lothlórien and completing his quest chain through 'Hilltop Assault.'\n7\tFind Bingo Boffin within the Haunted Inn, in the Dourstocks.\tBingo has arrived in Mirkwood, and he has naturally gone to the first tavern he could find: the Haunted Inn of the Dourstocks, west of Audaghaim.\n8\tLook into the distance from the bridge by the waterfall east of the Haunted Inn\030Look closely at the forgotten graveyard south of the Haunted Inn\030Look into the distance from the ruins of Audaghaim, south-east of the Haunted Inn\tBingo has asked you to find a number of locations near the Haunted Inn and look at them closely to help him learn about the area.\n9\tTalk to Bingo inside the Haunted Inn, in the Dourstocks\tBingo is by the fire inside the Haunted Inn, in the Dourstocks.\n",
[878]="7004A37E\n1\tSearch for Captain Lachír\tThe Captain was last seen turning south off the main road as they made their way farther into Udûn.\n2\tTalk to the soldiers\tYou should talk to the soldiers you found scrabbling among the rubble.\n3\tSearch among the rubble (total: 6)\tThe rummaging soldiers can be found east of the Foothold, south of Udûn's central road. Several men were left to rummage among refuse. You should help them check chests to speed up their burdensome task.\n4\tTalk to Iadan again\tThe rummaging soldiers can be found east of the Foothold, south of Udûn's central road. Now that you have helped with the rummaging some, you should try talking to the soldiers again.\n",
[879]="7005516D\n1\tApproach and interrupt Morgul will-binders in the Wracking-hall\tThe Wracking-hall can be found in the Circle of Death. You have encountered a number of focused will-binders in the Wracking-hall. If you interrupt their rituals, the nameless creatures can not be bound into the service of Gothmog.\n2\tApproach and interrupt Morgul will-binders in the Wracking-hall ([see journal]/4)\tThe Wracking-hall can be found in the Circle of Death. You have encountered a number of focused will-binders in the Wracking-hall. If you interrupt their rituals, the nameless creatures can not be bound into the service of Gothmog.\n3\tCompleted\tYou have disrupted the efforts of the Morgul will-binders to enslave more of the nameless creatures in the Wracking-hall.\n",
[880]="700011CD\n1\tCollect broken swords from Angmarim warriors (total: 5)\030Collect broken crossbows from Angmarim marksmen (total: 5)\tThe Angmarim are to the west of Gath Forthnír, near Carn Dûm. Areneth said that a display of strength could break the spirits of the Angmarim loyal to Mordor. He asked you to collect the weapons of those you defeat.\n2\tBring the weapons to Areneth\tAraneth is at Gath Forthnír, to the east of Carn Dûm. You must return to Araneth with the weapons which you captured.\n",
[881]="700687A8\n1\tDestroy rubble at the Shrine of He-Who-Sees-All (total: 8)\tRubble can be found at the ruined Shrine of He-Who-Sees-All in the Sail-haven of Umbar Baharbêl. Phenâsh has asked you to help clear the rubble at the ruined Shrine of He-Who-Sees-All.\n2\tTalk to Phenâsh at the Shrine of He-Who-Sees-All\tPhenâsh can be found at the ruined Shrine of He-Who-Sees-All in the Sail-haven of Umbar Baharbêl. You attempted to destroy the rubble at the Shrine of He-Who-Sees-All, but you were attacked by several frothing shrine-spirits. You should talk to Phenâsh.\n",
[882]="70047BC7\n1\tCollect hardy mushrooms in the Wastes (total: 4)\030Collect samples of blasted soil in the Wastes (total: 4)\030Collect a sample of water at the Slag-hills\tSoil and mushrooms can be found somewhere within the southern reaches of the Dead Marshes or upon the battle plain. The Slag-hills can be found due east of Haerondir. Mílgamel has asked you to seek samples of mushrooms, soil, and the brackish waters of the Slag-hills. You should obtain these samples and then return to her.\n2\tDeliver the samples to Mílgamel at Haerondir\tMílgamel can be found at Haerondir. You have gathered the samples that Mílgamel requested and should now return to her at Haerondir.\n",
[883]="7006C57D\n1\tObtain Ordâkhai warrior sashes from the Ordâkhai camp north of Jirush ([see journal]/4)\030Collect an Ordâkhai sounding horn\tAmalíbi sent you north-west to the Ordâkhai encampment to obtain sashes from the warriors, and a sounding horn from one of the mustering tents. You are to return to her at Ghalbûru after acquiring the items.\n2\tDeliver the sashes and the sounding horn to Amalíbi\tYou acquired the sashes and the sounding horn. Return to Amalíbi and show her you have the items.\n3\tPlace sashes on the Ordâkhai corpses near their south-east encampment\tAmalíbi directed you to the outskirts of the Ordâkhai encampment in the south-east and find the staged attack Amalíbi's forces provided. Place the sashes on the defeated Ordâkhai.\n4\tFind a spot to hide in a nearby bush and blow the horn\tWith the sashes placed, you should find a spot where you can watch what transpires when you blow the sounding horn.\n5\tSpeak with Bosóta in your hiding spot\tAfter blowing the horn, Captain Khârdu recognized the horn as Bosóta's. You need to speak with Bosóta and tell him to explain the tale to plant the seeds of rebellion among the Ordâkhai.\n6\tReturn to Amalíbi at Ghalbûru\tThe ruse was successful and Bosóta Dôlo played his part well. You should return to Amalíbi and inform her of the success.\n",
[884]="700000B2\n1\tUse Maggot's Mushrooms (total: 3)\tAtherol Took, a very accomplished burglar, is at Adso's Camp, west of the town of Bree. You have been told to speak with Atherol Took if you wish to become a better burglar.\n2\tBring Maggot's Mushrooms to Atherol Took\tAtherol Took is at Adso's Camp on the Great East Road, between Bree and Buckland. Atherol is waiting to speak with you about your expedition to Farmer Maggot's farm.\n",
[885]="7002EFEA\n1\tTalk to the Riders Four in Snowbourn\tUlf, Léofdag, and Hutha are waiting near the stables. Burnoth asked you to inform his Riders that he would meet you and them at Reeve Fastred's camp in the Sutcrofts.\n2\tTalk to Ulf to ride out into the Sutcrofts to meet Fastred\tUlf the Reaver is at the stables of Snowbourn. You should speak with Ulf the Reaver when you are ready to depart for Fastred's camp.\n3\tTalk to Burnoth outside the Mead Hall of Snowbourn\tBurnoth is outside the Mead Hall of Snowbourn. You should speak with Burnoth regarding the experience in the Sutcrofts.\n",
[886]="7003578A\n1\tDefeat Orc-smiths in Drû Vádokan (total: 3)\030Destroy White Hand forges (total: 2)\030Smother Orc-fires (total: 3)\tOrc-smiths and their tools can be found inside Drû Vádokan in north-west Balewood. Barallas has asked that you defeat the Orc-smiths in the Balewood and shatter their tools in hopes that their flames and axes will no longer be used against the inhabitants of the forest.\n2\tTalk to Barallas outside Drû Vádokan\tBarallas can be found to the east of Drû Vádokan. You have dealt a crippling blow to the smiths of Isengard within the Balewood. Their tools are shattered, their numbers thinned, and their fires extinguished.\n",
[887]="7002BD50\n1\tComplete Dargnákh's Rage in the Dargnákh Unleashed 3-man instance\030Complete Protecting the Forest in the Fangorn's Edge 3-man instance\030Complete Into the Pit of Abomination in the Pits of Isengard 3-man instance\tAndras has asked you to enter the Ring of Isengard, the eaves of Fangorn, and the Pits of Isengard and disrupt Saruman's war-efforts.\n2\tTalk to Andras at the Ox-clan encampment\tAndras is at the Ox-clan encampment in Nan Curunír. You should return to Andras with news of your successes.\n3\tComplete Ringing of the Hammer in the Foundry 6-man instance\tAndras has asked you to enter Saruman's Foundry, defeat the wizard's acolyte, Penrith, and destroy the forge to prevent more weapons of evil power from coming into existence.\n4\tTalk to Andras at the Ox-clan encampment in Nan Curunír\tAndras is at the Ox-clan encampment in Nan Curunír. You should return at once to Andras with news of your success and your discovery within Saruman's Foundry.\n5\tComplete The Rings of Isengard in the Tower of Isengard 12-man Raid\tAndras suggested only one course of action to remove the threat of Saruman's rings: enter Orthanc, face Saruman, take the rings, and destroy them.\n6\tTalk to Andras at the Ox-clan encampment\tAndras is at the Ox-clan encampment in Nan Curunír. You should return to Andras and tell him that Saruman's rings of power have been destroyed.\n",
[888]="7005A639\n1\tDefeat Moria Warg-riders at Târ-kútoz\tMoria Warg-riders can be found roaming around Târ-kútoz. Defeating these Warg-riders will help the dwarves at Ashmargathâl.\n2\tDefeat Moria Warg-riders (total: 5)\tMoria Warg-riders can be found roaming around Târ-kútoz. Defeating these Warg-riders will help the dwarves at Ashmargathâl.\n3\tCompleted\tYou have weakened the Warg-riders of Târ-kútoz.\n",
[889]="70037152\n1\tTalk to Ordlac in the Mead Hall of Oserley\tThane Ordlac is in the Mead Hall of Oserley. Dudsig instructed you to return at once to Thane Ordlac.\n",
[890]="7002CA86\n1\tFind the wanderer's trail outside Ost Celebrant\tCabed has sent you to track down a mysterious invader's trail. The trail ends at the bridge to Ost Celebrant, but Cabed is unsure where it begins.\n2\tExamine the boot-print\tCabed has sent you to track down a mysterious invader's trail. The trail ends at the bridge to Ost Celebrant, but Cabed is unsure where it begins.\n3\tFollow the trail of boot-prints\tCabed has sent you to track down a mysterious invader's trail. The trail ends at the bridge to Ost Celebrant, but Cabed is unsure where it begins.\n4\tFollow the trail of boot-prints\tCabed has sent you to track down a mysterious invader's trail. The trail ends at the bridge to Ost Celebrant, but Cabed is unsure where it begins.\n5\tFollow the trail of boot-prints\tCabed has sent you to track down a mysterious invader's trail. The trail ends at the bridge to Ost Celebrant, but Cabed is unsure where it begins.\n6\tExamine the glint in the distance\tYou should examine the glint you saw in the distance.\n7\tTalk to Cabed\tCabed is atop a small hill along the southern road in Parth Celebrant. You should bring the twisted blade to Cabed.\n",
[891]="7000371A\n1\tTalk to Cal Sprigley in Archet\tCal Sprigley can be found north of the ruins of The Mad Badger Inn in Archet. After spiders attacked his farm, Cal Sprigley and his wife fled to the safety of Archet. Atli Spider-bane has asked you to speak with the farmer.\n2\tCollect Sprigley's seed bag\030Collect Sprigley's strongbox\030Collect Sprigley's bow\tCal Sprigley's farm is south of Bronwe's Folly. Cal Sprigley has asked you to go to his farm and recover his strongbox, seed sack, and bow. With these things, he might be able to make a fresh start.\n3\tBring the seed bag, bow, and strongbox to Cal Sprigley\tCal Sprigley and his wife await you north of the ruins of The Mad Badger Inn in Archet. Cal and Holly Sprigley are waiting in Archet for the possessions you recovered from their spider-infested farm. You should return to them at once.\n",
[892]="70040380\n1\tFrightened townsfolk can be found in Dínadab in northern Lamedon. You should question townsfolk about the sighting of corsairs.\t\n2\tLook eastward for signs of Corsairs from atop the ridge\tThe ridge that may offer a view of the Corsair camp can be found to the east of Dínadab. You should look over the ridge towards the east. NOTE: This quest requires emotes.\n3\tFind the watchman and tell him about the Corsairs\tThe Watchman of Dínadab can be found standing outside of his home in northern Lamedon. You should speak with the watchman.\n4\tAsk the watchman for help in rescuing Fuirion\tThe Watchman of Dínadab can be found standing outside of his home in northern Lamedon. You should speak with the watchman.\n5\tSpeak with Gladion\tGladion stands outside the Watchman's home in Dínadab in northern Lamedon. You should speak with Gladion about Fuirion.\n",
[893]="70015E4B\n1\tDefeat Nethgarch, Worm-sire\tPembar is north-east of Echad Eregion and south-east of Glâd Ereg. Faenhilith has asked you to travel to Pembar and slay the worm-sire Nethgarch.\n2\tTalk to Faenhilith at Echad Eregion\tFaenhilith is in Echad Eregion, south-west of Pembar. You should return to Faenhilith with news of your victory against Nethgarch.\n",
[894]="7003E44E\n1\tSearch for the elder Huorn\tThe elder Huorn can be found in northern Fangorn Forest. Quickbeam's Huorn would greatly benefit from your aid in defending an elder Huorn of Fangorn.\n2\tTalk to Quickbeam's Huorn\tQuickbeam's Huorn is at your side or can be called from the depths of the forest. The elder Huorn's attackers have been quelled and it is now safe for it to wander the woods freely again.\n",
[895]="7005314C\n1\tInvestigate Lúlstrok\tLúlstrok can be found in the north-western reaches of the Gladden Fields. A bunting has delivered a message on Radagast's behalf asking you to investigate and drive out the Orkish presence in the Gladden Fields.\n2\tSabotage siege-tower wheels in Lúlstrok (total: 8)\tSiege-towers can be found in Lúlstrok. Aware that the Shapag-hai have siege-towers for some as of yet known purpose, you have been advised to sabotage the Orcs' siege-towers and keep them from inflicting more harm on the Gladden Fields.\n3\tFind and defeat the leader of the Shapag-hai in Lúlstrok\tThe leader of the Shapag-hai can be found somewhere in Lúlstrok. You should seek out and defeat the leader of the Shapag-hai in Lúlstrok.\n4\tDeliver tidings of the Shapag-hai's defeat to the bunting\tThe bunting can be found near Lúlstrok in the Gladden Fields. You have done much to repel the Shapag-hai in the Gladden Fields, and you should now return to the bunting and send it to inform Radagast that you have drive out the Orkish presence in the Gladden Fields.\n",
[896]="700346C2\n1\tCollect farm tools (total: 4)\030Repair broken fences (total: 6)\tSome of the wooden fences around Thrymm's Farm are broken or in need of repair, and there are tools scattered about the farm. All of the tools and broken fences can be found in the fields.\n2\tThe tools you picked up should be returned to Oter to be put away properly. He can be found by the large barn near the centre of Thrymm's Farm.\t\n",
})
